caos-expr: collapse the grammar onto a typed `--base`; add :docker=/:hash=

Checkpoint 2B of the typed-argument work (design/flake-inputs.md). The
`.caos-expr` surface no longer has a positional image or a `--`: a `run`/
`curry` is now `verb --base:<type>=<image> [--k…]`, where the reserved
`--base` names the worker to run (or curry onto), typed like any other arg.
This retires the last shape-sniffing on that surface — the image's kind is
the operator's explicit choice, never guessed from the value.

Arg-type vocabulary (crates/caos/src/lib.rs, parse_arg/ArgType):
  - :tree= -> :hash=, generalized from tree-only to a tree OR blob by oid.
  - new :docker=ref, stored as the blob `docker://<ref>` (the representation
    the server and base_arg_entry already expect).
  Both wired into build_arg_entries (CLI/worker args) and the evaluator.

Evaluator (crates/caos/src/eval.rs):
  - eval_command scans the tokens after the verb for the one named `base`
    (no positional, no `--`); the rest are ordinary args.
  - resolve_expr_image -> resolve_expr_base, dispatching on the explicit
    ArgType (docker / hash / path / $VAR) instead of sniffing.
  - resolve_expr_args handles :docker= and :hash=. Module grammar doc
    updated.

Migrated every .caos-expr to the new grammar: all 14 committed ones (the
root, std/, and std/*/ — including the multi-line curry/variable form in
std/llm-step), plus the fixtures that tests write at runtime in
tests/{eval-path,secrets,deep-deps}/cli.sh.

Deliberately NOT touched, so this stays isolated and low-risk: the CLI and
worker `caos` grammar and their sniffers (resolve_run_image /
resolve_cli_image). `caos-cli run <dir>` and `caos curry <img>` keep their
positional form for now; collapsing them (and typing the map-then image
positions) is checkpoint 2C.

No redeploy needed: the collapse produces byte-identical arg trees (same
base + args entries), so every seed key held and the outer stack kept
answering during the suite. Only direct dev use of a stale deployed
caos-cli against the new .caos-expr files would want `nix build && caosd up`.

Suite: 33/33 green (no redeploy).
